# #5841, reproduced: a stale duplicate of the donor arms after the split; ClaimRowAsync
# writes row + 1 and supersedes the bump, and its epoch-only write of a moved key is
# allocated above the receiver's close head.
MODULE: HandOffBoundStaleDonorArmsAfterSplit5841
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: #5841 exactly: the claim reads the row and writes row + 1 with no split sequence, and the split bumps only if its own activation armed
PERTURBS: DupClaim
BOUNDS: WithStaleDonor = TRUE, WithPreArm = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ IF rowSeq > 0
       THEN /\ dst' = "stale"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the claim does not check the split sequence.
    /\ IF FALSE
       THEN /\ dst' = "stale"
--- END

--- FIND
SplitBumps(read) == read > 0
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only an armed splitting activation bumps.
SplitBumps(read) == liveArmed
--- END
